 "limits": [
  "the walk is scope-local: a read of the same object in a callee is E630's arm, not this one, and a global read outside the function is out of scope by construction",
  "the receiver is identified by its leftmost name, so `a[b]['k']` and `a['k']` share a receiver -- depth is on every access so the reader can separate them",
  "an access whose node starts on the counted line is the same access E633 priced; it is published here with side `at_the_dead_line` and never counted as a neighbour",
  "aliasing is followed one hop inside the function body only",
  "a computed key reads some key and cannot be decided as this one, so it is published as a residual with its side instead of being folded into the same-key count",
  "a zero unnamed count is only a measurement because every row publishes how many accesses of that receiver the walker saw in the function body"
 ],
 "verdict": "no_counted_read_line_names_this_key_in_an_unrecognised_form_anywhere_in_the_function_that_holds_it_so_E633_line_scoped_census_and_E632_node_count_both_stand",
 "answer": "Across the 13 counted read line(s), the walker saw 230 access(es) of the same receiver(s) in the function bodies (44 of them recognised reads of the key). Not one is an unnamed entry read of the key on either side of the dead line (0 before / 0 after); the residual is 30 computed-key read(s) at the receiver's own level (8 before / 21 after), which read some key and cannot be decided as this one."
}
